      "score": 21.0,
      "latest_at": "2026-10-27T15:54:28.019914+00:00",
      "representative": {
        "title": "Deep-Microscopic Photonic Bandstructure of a Two-Dimensional Honeycomb Lattice",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33709",
        "source": "arXiv 光学与光子学 (physics.optics)",
        "published_at": "2026-10-27T04:00:00+00:00",
        "score": 65.3,
        "summary": "arXiv:2610.33709v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Conventional descriptions of light in materials rely on macroscopic models that average the optical response over the microscopic lattice structures. These models are deployed in the semi-clas",
        "zh_full": "材料中光的传统描述依赖于宏观模型，这些模型对微观晶格结构上的光学响应取平均。这些模型在半经典极限下使用，此时多个晶格位点上的集体局域响应是足够的。然而，它们无法捕捉完整的空间色散，这需要晶格分辨的光描述。作者通过基于麦克斯韦哈密顿量及其特征方程，提出一种深层微观非局域光子理论来解决这一局限。（原文在此处截断）",
